@startuml 01_component
title Adaptive-Bitrate Live Streaming Camera - components (as implemented, week 3)
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

node "Raspberry Pi 4 Model B (Raspberry Pi OS Lite 64-bit)" {
  component "systemd\nabr-hls.service" as SVC
  package "FFmpeg 7.1 process (scripts/run_abr.sh)" {
    component "Capture\nV4L2 MJPEG 1280x720@30\nALSA plughw:1,0" as CAP
    component "Scaler / splitter\n720p | 540p (960x540) | 360p" as SPL
    component "3 x h264_v4l2m2m\n2500k | 1200k | 500k\nGOP = 30" as ENC
    component "AAC encoder 128k\n(software)" as AAC
    component "HLS muxer (fMP4)\n1 s segments, master.m3u8" as MUX
  }
  database "tmpfs\n/dev/shm/hls" as RAM
  component "Nginx\n/hls/ (no-cache, CORS)" as NGX
  component "bcm2835-codec\n(/dev/video11)\nshared H.264 HW block" as HW
  component "Linux tc tbf\n(wlan0 test shaper)" as TC
}
node "USB devices" {
  component "UVC webcam + USB mic" as CAM
}
node "Client laptop (browser)" {
  component "hls.js player\nABR controller + EWMA estimator" as HLS
  component "Test logger\n(CSV: level, estimate, buffer, latency)" as LOG
}
CAM --> CAP : V4L2 / ALSA
CAP --> SPL : decoded frames
SPL --> ENC
ENC ..> HW : 3 jobs / frame (shared)
CAP --> AAC : PCM 48 kHz
ENC --> MUX
AAC --> MUX
MUX --> RAM : segments + playlists
RAM --> NGX
NGX --> TC : HTTP
TC --> HLS : Wi-Fi (limited 5 -> 0.7 Mbit/s)
HLS --> LOG
SVC ..> CAP : starts at boot (53 s to video)
@enduml
